WEBVTT

00:00:00.469 --> 00:00:05.165
Welcome to Alaventra. Rank in
search. Get recommended by AI.

00:00:06.143 --> 00:00:11.368
In tutorial 6.6, you'll send a
finished page to your CMS as a draft,

00:00:11.418 --> 00:00:13.378
then publish it live when you're ready.

00:00:14.388 --> 00:00:19.893
First, open the report of a written page.
On Content, click Report next to the page.

00:00:21.363 --> 00:00:26.338
Scroll down to Publish to your
CMS. Pages go as drafts by default,

00:00:26.388 --> 00:00:28.813
so nothing goes public by accident.

00:00:28.863 --> 00:00:33.146
A page that didn't pass its quality
check can't be sent until it's fixed.

00:00:34.150 --> 00:00:38.225
If you've connected more than one
CMS, choose one under Send to.

00:00:38.275 --> 00:00:40.813
Then click Send to CMS as draft.

00:00:42.650 --> 00:00:45.825
Once the page is there,
its status shows the draft,

00:00:45.875 --> 00:00:47.905
and the button reads Update the draft.

00:00:49.171 --> 00:00:52.147
History lists every send,
who made it, and when.

00:00:54.125 --> 00:00:58.743
When the page is ready to go public,
an owner or admin clicks Publish live.

00:01:00.650 --> 00:01:05.222
Tick that you've read the page and want
it public, then confirm with Publish live.

00:01:07.675 --> 00:01:11.433
Now the status shows Live, and the
page is tracked from that moment.

00:01:13.625 --> 00:01:16.425
Published it yourself in your CMS instead?

00:01:16.475 --> 00:01:19.000
On the draft, click Check if it is live,

00:01:19.050 --> 00:01:22.019
and Alaventra checks the
page and starts tracking it.

00:01:23.008 --> 00:01:27.483
So, open the written page report,
send it to your CMS as a draft,

00:01:27.533 --> 00:01:30.784
publish it live when you're
ready, and check that it is live.

00:01:31.768 --> 00:01:36.718
Your page is in your CMS. Next, read
a written page before you publish it,

00:01:36.768 --> 00:01:38.772
in tutorial 6.7.
